{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>You shall not make for yourselves idols.</b> He calls the celestial powers that are worshipped 'elilim' from the root אילות (strength), and he did not say אילים but אלילים to testify to the paucity of their power — for although they are great, they are not of themselves but only from something other than themselves. And after he mentioned 'elilim,' which are the supernal powers, he mentioned 'pesel' (graven image) and 'matzevah' (standing stone), which are the work of human hands made to receive those powers. And the reason he mentioned the matter of idolatry in this passage — the Rabbis, blessed be their memory, interpreted it as referring to one who sells himself to an idolater: Scripture speaks of this, so that he should not say, 'Since my master worships idols, I too will worship idols; since my master uncovers nakedness, I too will uncover nakedness; since my master desecrates Sabbaths, I too will desecrate Sabbaths; since my master sheds blood, I too will shed blood' — Scripture therefore says, 'You shall not make for yourselves idols.'" "<b>And a figured stone you shall not place.</b> Even for the sake of Heaven. It was the custom of idolaters to decorate a stone with a beautiful design and place the stone before the image and prostrate themselves upon it before it; and this is like the matter of the matzevah, which the Torah forbade even for the sake of Heaven. And likewise, the planting of a tree beside the altar, for all this was the practice of idol-worshippers. And they interpreted in the Sifra: 'in your land — to prostrate upon it': in your land you do not prostrate, but you do prostrate upon the stones that are in the Temple."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {1 "לשמים resolved as 'for the sake of Heaven' based on the well-known halakhic idiom and the parallel with the matzevah prohibition in Deuteronomy 16:22."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:28:35.123213965Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}